  "result": "I haven't changed any code yet. The plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\defaults-configured-through-default-map-dreamy-flask.md`. The `ExitPlanMode` tool isn't available in this session, so I can't request approval the normal way. Please confirm here and I'll implement it.\n\n**Cause:** `Context.__init__` in `src/click/core.py:392` gives a subcommand's context the parent's whole `default_map`. It should give it the entry for that subcommand's name. With `{\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}`, the `runserver` context looks for `port` at the top level and doesn't find it. This contradicts the nested `default_map` in `docs/commands.md`. The parameter lookup code is already correct once the context holds the right map.\n\n**Planned changes:**\n1. In `src/click/core.py`, change line 392 to `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. The existing guards stay.\n2. Add tests in `tests/test_defaults.py`. They cover:\n   - a nested subcommand default;\n   - top-level keys not leaking into subcommands;\n   - a group inside a group;\n   - an explicit `context_settings` `default_map` still overriding;\n   - falling back to the parameter default when the subcommand key is missing.\n3. Add an entry at the top of `CHANGES.md`.\n\n**Verification:** I'll run the affected test files and then the full suite.\n\nOne behaviour change to be aware of: a top-level key such as `{\"debug\": True}` will no longer apply to subcommands that have a `debug` parameter. Defaults for a subcommand have to sit under its name.",
